---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { skillUrl, u } from '../lib/url';
import { CV_PDF } from '../../scripts/cv-pdf-render.mjs';

const sections = [
  { id: 'stack', title: 'Stack' },
  { id: 'fonts', title: 'Type' },
  { id: 'tokens', title: 'Design system' },
  { id: 'nolojs', title: 'NoLoJS' },
  { id: 'analytics', title: 'Analytics' },
  { id: 'print', title: 'Print and PDF' },
] as const;
type SectionId = (typeof sections)[number]['id'];
const num = (id: SectionId) => String(sections.findIndex((s) => s.id === id) + 1).padStart(2, '0');
const title = (id: SectionId) => sections.find((s) => s.id === id)!.title;
---
<Base title="Colophon" current="colophon" description="How this site is built: principles, stack, type, tokens, and privacy.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head mgrid">
      <p class="kicker m"><span class="usq" aria-hidden="true"></span>Colophon</p>
      <div>
        <h1>How this site is built</h1>
        <p class="lede">The site is part of my work. Three principles decide each detail.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="panels" aria-label="Design principles">
      <div class="panel panel-precise">
        <h2>Precise</h2>
        <p class="ratio tnum">1.125 · 1.25 · 1.414</p>
        <p class="explain">Every size, gap, and column comes from a ratio. The type steps by 1.125 on phones and 1.25 on large screens. The CV page and the print CV use the A4 ratio, 1 : 1.414.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel panel-unsq">
        <span class="usq usq-turn" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h2><span class="big">One</span> <span class="rest">unsquare per view</span></h2>
        <p class="explain">Each screen gets one deliberate break: a rotation, a bleed, or a jump in scale. One break makes a focal point. Two breaks fight for it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel panel-proof">
        <h2><span class="bold">Proof,</span> <span class="light">not claims</span></h2>
        <p class="explain">I do not rate my skills with bars or stars. The type, the grid, and the tokens on this page are the evidence. <a href="https://github.com/usqr/usqr">Read the source</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sec mgrid" id="stack" aria-labelledby="stack-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num('stack')}</span><h2 id="stack-h">{title('stack')}</h2></div>
      <p class="prose-p">Astro makes static HTML and CSS from Markdown posts and one CV data file. No framework runs in the browser. GitHub Actions builds the site and GitHub Pages hosts it.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="sec mgrid" id="fonts" aria-labelledby="fonts-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num('fonts')}</span><h2 id="fonts-h">{title('fonts')}</h2></div>
      <p class="prose-p">LatoVar for text and Bitter for headings and numerals. LatoVar is <a href={u('/sidequests/lato-var/')}>my variable build of Lato 3</a>: one file has each weight from 100 to 900. Bitter has oldstyle figures, so the numbers sit in the line of text. I host the files myself. I cut them to English and Polish letters, so each file is about 21–39 KB.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="sec mgrid" id="tokens" aria-labelledby="tokens-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num('tokens')}</span><h2 id="tokens-h">{title('tokens')}</h2></div>
      <p class="prose-p">One token file holds the colors, type sizes, and spacing. Light and dark themes use the same tokens. The ornament comes from my unsquare brandbook: the 45° lattice, the corner band, and the mark. See the skill <a href={skillUrl('design-tokens')}>Design tokens</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="sec mgrid" id="nolojs" aria-labelledby="nolojs-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num('nolojs')}</span><h2 id="nolojs-h">{title('nolojs')}</h2></div>
      <p class="prose-p">Every page works without JavaScript. Links, layout, print, and the light and dark themes are plain HTML and CSS. Two small scripts add extras: a switch for the light or dark theme, and Cmd/Ctrl+P for the print CV. Without JavaScript, the theme follows your system setting.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="sec mgrid" id="analytics" aria-labelledby="analytics-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num('analytics')}</span><h2 id="analytics-h">{title('analytics')}</h2></div>
      <p class="prose-p">I count visits with GoatCounter. It sets no cookies and keeps no personal data. Without JavaScript, an image counts the visit.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="sec mgrid" id="print" aria-labelledby="print-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num('print')}</span><h2 id="print-h">{title('print')}</h2></div>
      <p class="prose-p">The <a href={u('/cv/')}>print CV</a> is two A4 pages with a print stylesheet. The page grid uses root-2 parts, and each page has a footer with my name and the page number. The build makes <a href={u(`/${CV_PDF}`)} download>the PDF</a> from the same page.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
